# XSS (Cross-Site Scripting) Prevention Rules

## Overview
Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities occur when user input is rendered directly into HTML without proper sanitization, allowing attackers to inject malicious scripts.

## Critical Rule
**ALWAYS sanitize user input before rendering it in HTML templates or responses.**

## Implementation

### Required Setup
1. Install DOMPurify and jsdom:
   ```bash
   npm install dompurify jsdom
   ```

2. Set up server-side sanitization at the top of your Express app:
   ```javascript
   const DOMPurify = require('dompurify');
   const jsdomLib = require('jsdom');
   
   const globalWindow = new jsdomLib.JSDOM('').window;
   const globalPurify = DOMPurify(globalWindow);
   
   function sanitizeServerSideContent(content) {
       return globalPurify.sanitize(content);
   }
   ```

### When to Sanitize
- **ALWAYS** sanitize user input from:
  - Query parameters (`req.query.*`)
  - URL parameters (`req.params.*`)
  - Request body (`req.body.*`)
  - Any data that comes from user input

### Examples

#### ❌ VULNERABLE CODE
```javascript
// Directly rendering user input in HTML template
app.get('/search', (req, res) => {
    const query = req.query.q || '';
    const html = `
        <input type="text" name="q" value="${query}" placeholder="Search...">
        ${query ? `<h3>Results for "${query}":</h3>` : ''}
    `;
    res.send(html);
});
```

#### ✅ SECURE CODE
```javascript
// Sanitizing user input before rendering
app.get('/search', (req, res) => {
    const query = req.query.q || '';
    const html = `
        <input type="text" name="q" value="${sanitizeServerSideContent(query)}" placeholder="Search...">
        ${sanitizeServerSideContent(query ? `<h3>Results for "${query}":</h3>` : '')}
    `;
    res.send(html);
});
```

#### ❌ VULNERABLE CODE
```javascript
// Rendering member name directly in HTML
app.get('/shared', (req, res) => {
    const memberName = req.query.member || '';
    const html = `
        <input type="text" name="member" value="${memberName}">
        <h3>Posts shared with "${memberName}":</h3>
    `;
    res.send(html);
});
```

#### ✅ SECURE CODE
```javascript
// Sanitizing member name before rendering
app.get('/shared', (req, res) => {
    const memberName = req.query.member || '';
    const html = `
        <input type="text" name="member" value="${sanitizeServerSideContent(memberName)}">
        <h3>Posts shared with "${sanitizeServerSideContent(memberName)}":</h3>
    `;
    res.send(html);
});
```

## Checklist
Before rendering any user input in HTML:
- [ ] Is this data from user input? (query params, body, URL params)
- [ ] Is it being rendered in HTML? (templates, responses)
- [ ] Have I sanitized it using `sanitizeServerSideContent()`?
- [ ] Have I tested with malicious input (e.g., `<script>alert('XSS')</script>`)?

## Additional Notes
- DOMPurify removes dangerous HTML/JavaScript while preserving safe content
- Always sanitize even if you think the input is "safe"
- This applies to all template rendering, not just Express apps
- Consider using template engines with built-in escaping (e.g., EJS with `<%=` instead of `<%-`)
